  "identifier": "open-ecg-digitizer",
  "name": "Open-ECG-Digitizer",
  "description": "Open-source tool for automatically extracting raw time-series voltage data from paper ECG images — scanned or photographed. Uses semantic segmentation to handle perspective distortions, variable image quality, and any subset of the standard 12 leads. Outputs values in microvolts, configurable via YAML. Enables digitisation of historical paper ECG archives for clinical research and AI model training at scale. Published in npj Digital Medicine 2026 (Stenhede et al.). v1.9.3, 87 stars, Python, Akershus University Hospital AIM Lab (Norway). CC BY-SA 4.0.",
